    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Since you are told to assume <span data-math=\"p\"></span> is true and <span data-math=\"q\"></span> is false, you only need one row of possible truth values in your truth table.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"p\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"q\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"p \\leftrightarrow q\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>F</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span data-math=\"p \\leftrightarrow q\"></span></p>\n<p>A biconditional is true when the two statements have the same truth value. Otherwise, it is false.</p>\n<p>Since <span data-math=\"p\"></span> and <span data-math=\"q\"></span> have different truth values, the biconditional is false. Write an F in the last column.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"p\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"q\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"p \\leftrightarrow q\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>F</td>\n<td>F</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The statement is false because there is an F in the last column.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "False\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-math=\"p\">p</span></th>\n<th><span data-math=\"q\">q</span></th>\n<th><span data-math=\"{p} \\leftrightarrow {q}\">{p} \\leftrightarrow {q}</span></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>T</td>\n<td>F</td>\n<td><b>F</b></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
